PHASE 31 — Security Audit, Access Control, Data Protection, and Production Hardening

Goal:
Perform a full security audit and hardening pass across the entire Habiba Nabil Arabic Academy platform before production launch.

Important:
Do not add new business features in this phase.
Do not redesign the app.
Do not change database provider.
The active database is Supabase PostgreSQL.
The app must not use Replit internal @base database.
Focus only on security, access control, data protection, upload safety, payment safety, and production readiness.

==================================================
PART 1 — AUTHENTICATION SECURITY
==================================================

Review and harden authentication.

Check:
- Password hashing is secure.
- Demo passwords are only for development/demo.
- Sessions/JWT are secure.
- Logout properly clears session.
- Protected pages require login.
- Unauthorized users are redirected safely.
- No protected data appears before auth check.
- Login errors do not reveal whether email exists.
- Rate limit login attempts if practical.
- Add account lockout or cooldown if practical.

Acceptance:
- Logged-out user cannot access protected dashboards.
- Student cannot open Owner pages.
- Parent cannot open Owner pages.
- Academy partner cannot open Owner pages.
- Wrong password gives safe generic error.
- Logout works fully.

==================================================
PART 2 — ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL
==================================================

Audit role permissions.

Roles:
- OWNER_TEACHER
- STUDENT
- PARENT
- ACADEMY_PARTNER

Rules:
- Owner/Teacher can access all management pages.
- Student can only access their own data.
- Parent can only access linked child/children.
- Academy Partner can only access their own briefs.
- Public users can only access public pages and public test flows.

Check all routes:
- /owner/*
- /student/*
- /parent/*
- /academy/*
- /api/*
- /level-test/*
- /checkout/*
- /thank-you/*
- upload/download routes

Acceptance:
- Direct URL access is blocked if role is wrong.
- API routes enforce the same permissions as pages.
- Frontend hiding buttons is not enough; backend must check permissions.

==================================================
PART 3 — DATA OWNERSHIP CHECKS
==================================================

Audit data ownership.

Student must only access:
- own homework
- own scenario
- own reviews/tests
- own materials
- own notifications
- own package balance
- own bookings
- own progress
- own level checks if linked

Parent must only access:
- linked child homework
- linked child scenarios
- linked child reviews
- linked child materials
- linked child progress
- linked child package balance
- linked child bookings

Academy Partner must only access:
- briefs submitted by same academy partner account

Acceptance:
- Student A cannot open Student B homework/result URLs.
- Parent A cannot open another parent’s child data.
- Academy Partner A cannot open Academy Partner B brief.
- Unauthorized access returns 403 or redirects safely.

==================================================
PART 4 — DATABASE AND SECRET SECURITY
==================================================

Check:
- DATABASE_URL is server-side only.
- DATABASE_URL_SESSIONPOOLER is server-side only.
- Ziina API key is server-side only.
- AI API keys are server-side only.
- Firebase service account is server-side only.
- No secrets are committed in source files.
- No secrets are printed in logs.
- Startup logs show only safe host names, never passwords.
- .env.example contains placeholders only.
- The app ignores Replit internal @base database.
- Supabase connection uses the correct resolver.
- Leading/trailing spaces in secrets are trimmed safely.

Acceptance:
- No full connection strings appear in frontend, browser, logs, or public files.
- System Health shows safe status only.
- No secret values are exposed.

==================================================
PART 5 — PAYMENT SECURITY
==================================================

Audit Ziina payment flow.

Rules:
- Never mark payment as paid from frontend redirect alone.
- Thank-you page can check Ziina status server-side.
- If payment is not confirmed, status remains pending_verification.
- Owner manual verification requires confirmation.
- Manual payment changes are audit logged.
- No card data is stored.
- Payment amount cannot be changed from frontend.
- Plan amount is calculated server-side from database/settings.
- Checkout reference should be secure and not guessable.

Check:
- Checkout order creation.
- Ziina payment intent creation.
- Payment status check.
- Owner payment dashboard.
- Manual mark paid/refunded/failed.
- Optional webhook route if present.

Acceptance:
- User cannot fake paid status by editing URL.
- User cannot change AED 1600 plan into AED 80 from frontend.
- Payment status changes are audit logged.

==================================================
PART 6 — UPLOAD SECURITY
==================================================

Audit all upload features.

Uploads may include:
- student speaking recordings
- scenario recordings
- level test speaking uploads
- homework files
- materials
- PDFs
- PowerPoint files
- images
- testimonial audio/video
- HTML materials

Rules:
- Validate MIME type.
- Validate extension.
- Validate file size.
- Block dangerous extensions:
  .php, .exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .msi, .dll, .ps1, .com, .scr
- Do not allow executable uploads.
- Do not trust filename from user.
- Generate safe stored filenames.
- Store original filename separately.
- Protect private uploads from unauthorized users.
- HTML material must be sandboxed or download-only.
- No uploaded HTML should run with app privileges.
- Audio/video should not autoplay.

Acceptance:
- Invalid files are rejected.
- Oversized files are rejected.
- Student cannot download another student’s private file.
- Parent cannot download unlinked child files.
- Public cannot access unapproved testimonial media.

==================================================
PART 7 — FREE LEVEL TEST SECURITY
==================================================

Audit Free Level Test and Quick Check.

Check:
- Public cannot view other attempts.
- Secure token/reference is used.
- Attempt snapshot cannot be modified by user.
- Correct answers are not exposed before submission.
- Users cannot skip locked steps.
- Refresh does not regenerate questions.
- File uploads are validated.
- Rate limit/spam protection if practical.
- Owner review pages are protected.

Acceptance:
- User cannot open another attempt by changing ID.
- User cannot see correct answers in frontend data before submitting.
- User cannot jump directly to Reading/Writing without proper progress.

==================================================
PART 8 — NOTIFICATION SECURITY
==================================================

Audit notifications.

Rules:
- Notification action URLs must respect permissions.
- Student notification links must only open own data.
- Parent notification links must only open linked child data.
- Academy links must only open own briefs.
- Owner links can open management pages.
- Mark-as-read must only affect the current user’s notifications.

Acceptance:
- User cannot read or mark another user’s notifications.
- Notification action buttons do not bypass route protection.

==================================================
PART 9 — AI SECURITY
==================================================

Audit AI tools.

Rules:
- AI API key is server-side only.
- AI output is draft/preview only.
- AI never auto-publishes homework, articles, scenarios, materials, or messages.
- AI usage logs do not expose secrets.
- Owner must approve/apply AI output.
- Regenerate limits work.
- AI provider can be disabled.
- If API key is missing, AI tools fail safely.

Acceptance:
- AI output cannot publish automatically.
- Student/Parent/Academy cannot access Owner AI tools.
- AI logs are Owner-only.

